export anchor MissionControlStyle:
    number: 306
    screen: OpsMonitor
    name: Mission control
    idea: A deep navy control room wall, a row of large countdown style clocks over a grid of numbered console panels with cyan corner brackets, nominal and caution wording and condensed caps.
    base: dark
    palette:
        night: #040a14, the page and the clock faces
        console: #0a1628, panel fill and swatches
        tile: #0e1d33, service tiles
        rule: #29486b, panel borders
        ink: #dbe8f5, text
        muted: #8fa8c4, labels and axes
        cyan: #59d6ff, clock digits, corner brackets, the requests line, p50, Recovered and the primary button
        amber: #ffb020, Caution, the incident panel, p95 and the open incident clock
        green: #4be08a, Nominal, Resolved and the live indicator
        red: #ff6b6b, the error line and Firing
        focus: #ffffff, a white focus outline with a cyan halo
    type:
        Condensed labels in Bahnschrift, DIN Alternate, Roboto Condensed,
        Arial Narrow, system-ui at 14px, and ui-monospace, SF Mono, Menlo,
        Consolas for clocks and figures. Clocks are 44px mono at 600 with a
        soft glow, the incident number 28px mono bold amber, panel titles
        12px caps tracked 0.2em, status words 13px bold caps tracked 0.12em.
    layout:
        A header bar holds BRIGHTWORK OPS over Production control in
        tracked caps, the apps as caps links with Ops boxed in cyan, and a
        Telemetry live line. The description runs as a tracked caps line.
        A row of four clock boxes follows, Station time 10.00.00, INC-0427
        open T+03.02 in amber, Billing back T+02.06 and Last deploy
        T+00.48, each with a note. Below sits a three column wall of
        console panels, each square with cyan L brackets at the corners and
        a numbered title such as Console 01 Services. Console 01 holds the
        services as a two by two grid of tiles with a 3px status top edge
        and billing full width, Console 02 the requests line on a 12 by 5
        grid with a ringed peak and peak and floor readouts, Console 03 the
        incident with an amber border, then Console 04 error rate, Console
        05 latency and Console 06 the event log, and Console 07 the deploy
        sequence across the full width in three columns. The wall goes to
        two columns below 1100px and one at phone width.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 12px gutters, 16px panel padding, 24px page padding.
    density: Medium dense. Four clocks and seven consoles on one wide wall.
    corners: Square panels with 14px cyan corner brackets, chamfered 8px corners on buttons.
    borders: 1px #29486b on panels and clocks, an amber border on the incident, 3px status top edges on tiles.
    shadows: A faint glow on the clock digits only, and a radial navy glow at the top of the page.
    icons:
        18px status shapes beside caps words, a ringed tick for Nominal, a
        triangle for Caution, a circular arrow for Recovered, a bolt for
        Firing, a tick for Resolved and a magnifier for Investigating.
    focus: A 2px white outline offset 3px with a 6px cyan halo.
    tone: Control room words, such as Console 04, Nominal, Caution, Event log, Deploy sequence and T plus clocks.
